      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those small, irregular holes are most likely caused by tears from overheating or drying leaf tissue, common issues in greenhouses. alternatively, this could be early-stage thrips damage, which often leaves tiny, silvery specks rather than large holes, and there may be tiny flies flying unseen. I recommend checking for insect fecal spots or red streaks on the underside of the leaves to confirm between tear damage and insect damage like thrips.",
